```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when promiscuous mode is enabled, the Receive All (RA) bit is set in the GMAC packet filter register, but when promiscuous mode is turned off, the RA bit is not cleared. This results in the device continuing to receive all network packets, even when it should only receive packets specifically addressed to it.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
value &= ~GMAC_PACKET_FILTER_RA;
```
Reason:
This line explicitly clears the Receive All (RA) bit in the GMAC packet filter register when promiscuous mode is turned off. By ensuring that the RA bit is cleared, the device will stop receiving all packets and will only receive those that are addressed to it or broadcast packets, thus correcting the unintended packet capture behavior.

